","note":"The story gallery names Mustafar and immediately describes the fleet landing at Black Sun’s cliffside facility; it is not merely a proposed destination."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e14","worldId":"nal-hutta","worldName":"Nal Hutta","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/eminence-episode-gallery","note":"The story gallery explicitly places Maul, Savage, and Vizsla before the Hutt Council on Nal Hutta. Jabba attends this meeting by hologram."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e14","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/eminence-episode-gallery","note":"The story gallery names the retreat to Jabba’s Tatooine palace, then confirms Maul and Vizsla’s forces arrive and enter that palace. Jabba’s earlier hologram on Nal Hutta is distinguished from this visit."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e18","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/the-jedi-who-knew-too-much-episode-gallery","note":"The story gallery explicitly places Anakin’s pursuit of Ahsoka at an opening into Coruscant’s underworld."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e03","worldId":"kamino","worldName":"Kamino","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/fugitive-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Fives and AZI-3 in Tipoca City. https://www.starwars.com/databank/tipoca-city identifies that city as the central hub of Kamino. The proposed later Coruscant transfer is excluded."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e09","worldId":"zardossa-stix","worldName":"Zardossa Stix","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/the-disappeared-part-ii-episode-gallery","note":"The story gallery places the captive queen’s arrival and the rescue pursuit on the desert moon Zardossa Stix. Bardotta’s abduction recap alone is not counted as a new scene."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e12","worldId":"force-planet","worldName":"Force planet (unnamed)","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/destiny-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery confirms Yoda’s landing on the unnamed world inside the nebula. The exact episode guide indexes it as Force Planet and explicitly says it has no specific name. This descriptive identity has no coordinates; Moraband is only Yoda’s next destination."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s07e07","worldId":"oba-diah","worldName":"Oba Diah","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/dangerous-debt-episode-guide","note":"The exact episode guide’s story gallery places the trio in the Pyke prison and stronghold; its location index identifies Pyke Stronghold. https://www.starwars.com/databank/pyke-stronghold locates that named fortress on Oba Diah. No recalled Martez-family events become new visits."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s07e08","worldId":"oba-diah","worldName":"Oba Diah","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/together-again-episode-guide","note":"The episode story gallery explicitly places Ahsoka’s sabotage in the Pyke complex on Oba Diah."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s07e08","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/together-again-episode-guide","note":"The episode story gallery explicitly confirms the trio’s return to Coruscant. Tracing Maul’s signal to Mandalore is not counted as Ahsoka visiting Mandalore."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s04e14","worldId":"carlac","worldName":"Carlac","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-clone-wars-rewatch-a-friend-in-need","note":"The exact episode rewatch explicitly places Lux’s ill-fated alliance with Death Watch on the frigid world of Carlac."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e02","worldId":"kenari","context":"flashback","worldName":"Kenari","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-episode-2-that-would-be-me-highlights","note":"Flashback: the episode highlights place young Kassa and the mining devastation on Kenari. This is not an adult Cassian visit."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e03","worldId":"kenari","context":"flashback","worldName":"Kenari","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-episode-3-reckoning-highlights","note":"Flashback: the episode highlights explicitly identify Kenari as the setting where young Cassian enters the crashed transport and is later rescued."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e08","worldId":"segra-milo","context":"surface","worldName":"Segra-Milo","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-episode-8-narkina-5-highlights","note":"The episode highlights place Saw Gerrera and his tense meeting with Luthen on Segra Milo, normalized here as Segra-Milo. No map position is supplied."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e11","worldId":"ferrix","context":"surface","worldName":"Ferrix","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-revisited-rewatch-season-1-arc-4","note":"The rewatch explicitly identifies the episode 11 scene on Ferrix in which B2EMO grieves Maarva and Brasso comforts him; this is not inferred from Cassian calling the planet."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e11","worldId":"niamos","worldName":"Niamos","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/andor/andor-episode-11-daughter-of-ferrix","note":"The exact episode guide indexes Niamos and describes the fugitives obtaining a ride back there. This is an episode/location association; no arrival time or travel sequence is assigned."},{"itemId":"andor-s01e11","worldId":"segra-milo","context":"orbit","worldName":"Segra-Milo","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-revisited-rewatch-season-1-arc-4","note":"The episode 11 rewatch places Luthen''s encounter with the Imperial arrestor cruiser in orbit above Segra-Milo after visiting Saw. Orbital action is included; no Cassian surface visit is implied."},{"itemId":"andor-s02e10","worldId":"naboo","context":"flashback","worldName":"Naboo","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-season-2-finale-episodes-10-11-12","note":"Flashback: the finale commentary identifies Naboo as the setting of young Kleya and Luthen''s explosive operation. The episode 10 guide places Kleya''s recollections alongside her hospital mission: https://www.starwars.com/series/andor/season-2-episode-10-episode-guide"},{"itemId":"andor-s02e12","worldId":"coruscant","context":"surface","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-season-2-finale-episodes-10-11-12","note":"The finale commentary locates the safehouse confrontation on Coruscant. The exact episode 12 synopsis identifies Cassian, Melshi, and Kleya escaping that assault with K-2SO: https://www.starwars.com/series/andor/season-2-episode-12-episode-guide"},{"itemId":"andor-s02e12","worldId":"mina-rau","context":"surface","worldName":"Mina-Rau","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/andor-season-2-finale-episodes-10-11-12","note":"The official finale commentary explicitly identifies the concluding field scene as Mina-Rau. This is a separate closing scene, not Cassian''s next mission destination."},{"itemId":"mandalorian-s03e02","worldId":"tatooine","context":"surface","worldName":"Tatooine","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-mandalorian-chapter-18-the-mines-of-mandalore-highlights","note":"The Chapter 18 highlights explicitly describe Din and Grogu stopping on Tatooine during Boonta Eve to obtain R5-D4 before their Mandalore expedition."},{"itemId":"mandalorian-s03e02","worldId":"kalevala","context":"surface","worldName":"Kalevala","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-mandalorian-chapter-18-the-mines-of-mandalore-highlights","note":"The Chapter 18 highlights locate Bo-Katan on her throne on Kalevala before she is summoned to rescue Din. This supports her parallel setting, not a continuous Din itinerary."},{"itemId":"mandalorian-s03e05","worldId":"adelphi","context":"surface","worldName":"Adelphi","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/star-wars-the-mandalorian-and-grogu-set-visit","note":"The official Adelphi Base set visit explicitly identifies the bar scene introducing live-action Garazeb Orrelios as Season 3, Chapter 21: The Pirate. No coordinates are supplied, and the later film is not added to the catalog."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s01e11","worldId":"vanqor","worldName":"Vanqor","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/dooku-captured-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes Dooku and the pursuing Jedi crash-landing on Vanqor, followed by the Jedi searching its caves.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s01e11","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/dooku-captured-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places Palpatine and his staff on Coruscant while they review Hondo''s ransom transmission. The pirates appear remotely; this is the Republic-side scene.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s02e01","worldId":"felucia","worldName":"Felucia","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/holocron-heist-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery opens with Obi-Wan, Anakin and Ahsoka fighting on Felucia before their evacuation.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s02e03","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/children-of-the-force-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places the Jedi Council reports and Anakin''s meeting with Palpatine on Coruscant.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s02e03","worldId":"rodia","worldName":"Rodia","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/children-of-the-force-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places Bane''s abduction in Kay-Tap on Rodia and describes Obi-Wan arriving at the child''s home. This is an enacted scene, not only the preceding Force vision.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s02e03","worldId":"naboo","worldName":"Naboo","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/children-of-the-force-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes Anakin and Ahsoka landing at Theed on Naboo and the trap for Bane in Jan-gwa.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e12","worldId":"dathomir","worldName":"Dathomir","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/nightsisters-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes Ventress returning to Dathomir and being received by Mother Talzin; it later records the Nightsisters returning there after their failed attack.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e13","worldId":"devaron","worldName":"Devaron","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/monster-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Savage''s attack on the Eedit Temple on Devaron, including combat with its clone and Jedi defenders.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e14","worldId":"dathomir","worldName":"Dathomir","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/witches-of-the-mist-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places Savage''s return to Mother Talzin''s lair on Dathomir after the betrayal. This is a present episode scene, not the Devaron surveillance recording.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e14","worldId":"toydaria","worldName":"Toydaria","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/witches-of-the-mist-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly describes Savage arriving at Toydaria''s palace, followed by Obi-Wan and Anakin. Later fighting aboard a frigate is also described above the world.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e17","worldId":"cato-neimoidia","worldName":"Cato Neimoidia","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/sabotage-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places Anakin and Ahsoka''s opening starfighter battle over Cato Neimoidia and among its bridge-city spires. This supports atmospheric action, not a claimed surface landing."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e06","worldId":"scipio","worldName":"Scipio","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/the-rise-of-clovis-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes the Core Five and Nix Card arguing in the Main Vault on Scipio. This scene follows the recap and is not inferred from the previous episode.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e06","worldId":"serenno","worldName":"Serenno","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/the-rise-of-clovis-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places the Dooku-side plotting scene on Serenno. Sidious participates remotely; this does not claim Sidious traveled to Serenno.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s01e13","worldId":"quell","worldName":"Quell","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/jedi-crash-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places the opening Republic cruiser battle high in Quell''s atmosphere, then describes departure from Quell. This is atmospheric combat, not a claimed surface landing."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s01e18","worldId":"naboo","worldName":"Naboo","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/mystery-of-a-thousand-moons-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Padme caring for infected clones on Naboo, and later the returning Jedi in its eastern swamps. This is separate from the Iego mission.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s02e04","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/senate-spy-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery opens with Anakin visiting Padme at her apartment on Coruscant before the spying mission.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e07","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/assassin-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly describes Padme, Ahsoka and their entourage returning to Coruscant with Aurra Sing in custody, where Anakin and Yoda meet them.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s03e10","worldId":"raxus","worldName":"Raxus","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/heroes-on-both-sides-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes Padme and Ahsoka arriving on Raxus and meeting Mina Bonteri at the landing platform. This is Raxus, not an inferred visit to Raxus Prime.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s04e13","worldId":"zygerria","worldName":"Zygerria","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/escape-from-kadavo-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places Dooku''s arrival and Queen Miraj''s palace scenes on Zygerria, alongside the separate rescue at Kadavo. It does not place the holographic Sidious there.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s04e19","worldId":"serenno","worldName":"Serenno","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/massacre-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Dooku in his Serenno lair ordering the attack, and later suffering Talzin''s remote spell there. These are separate from the fighting on Dathomir.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e02","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/a-war-on-two-fronts-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places the Jedi Council discussion on Coruscant. The Onderon resistance leaders report remotely; this does not imply they traveled to Coruscant.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e05","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/tipping-points-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Anakin and Obi-Wan on Coruscant while discussing Ahsoka''s remote request for assistance on Onderon.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s05e05","worldId":"florrum","worldName":"Florrum","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/tipping-points-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery describes Anakin piloting his starfighter to Florrum to ask Hondo to deliver missiles. The appearance is not inferred merely from Hondo''s later supply delivery."},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e01","worldId":"ringo-vinda","worldName":"Ringo Vinda","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/the-unknown-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery locates the battle on the immense ring station encircling Ringo Vinda, with cruiser medical scenes and a spacewalk. This is an orbital setting, not a planetary surface visit.","context":"orbit"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e02","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/conspiracy-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery places the assembled Jedi Council on Coruscant receiving Shaak Ti''s holographic report. Shaak Ti herself is remote; her presence is not assigned to Coruscant.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"clone-wars-s06e13","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/clone-wars/sacrifice-episode-gallery","note":"The episode gallery explicitly places Dooku''s landing and the Sith ritual on Coruscant. This supports the actual Sith-side scenes, independently of Yoda''s subsequent induced vision.","context":"surface"},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e01","worldId":"arcana","worldName":"Arcana","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-one-master-and-apprentice-episode-guide","note":"The exact episode guide places Ahsoka investigating an ancient temple on Arcana. No supported map position is assigned."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e01","worldId":"lothal","worldName":"Lothal","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-one-master-and-apprentice-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide explicitly places Governor Azadi’s monument dedication on Lothal."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e02","worldId":"lothal","worldName":"Lothal","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-two-toil-and-trouble-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide places Sabine recovering in the hospital in Lothal’s Capital City."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e02","worldId":"seatos","worldName":"Seatos","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-two-toil-and-trouble-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide places Baylan and Shin at an ancient site on Seatos."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e02","worldId":"corellia","worldName":"Corellia","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-two-toil-and-trouble-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide confirms Ahsoka and Hera meeting at the Corellian shipyard factory on Corellia, not merely planning a visit."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e03","worldId":"seatos","worldName":"Seatos","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-three-time-to-fly-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide confirms emergence from hyperspace at Seatos followed by descent and landing in the red-leaf forest."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e04","worldId":"seatos","worldName":"Seatos","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-four-fallen-jedi-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide places Sabine and Ahsoka repairing their ship in Seatos’s forests. Calculations to Peridea do not establish arrival there."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e05","worldId":"seatos","worldName":"Seatos","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/ahsoka-part-5-shadow-warrior-highlights","note":"The episode highlights explicitly describe Jacen sensing events beneath the Seatos oceans during Hera’s search."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e05","worldId":"mandalore","worldName":"Mandalore","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-five-shadow-warrior-episode-guide","note":"Vision / relived past: the episode guide transports Ahsoka into her Clone Wars battles, including the Siege of Mandalore. This is not present-day travel to Mandalore."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e06","worldId":"peridea","worldName":"Peridea","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-six-far-far-away-episode-guide","note":"The exact episode guide confirms the craft arriving at Peridea, in another galaxy. No placement in the atlas galaxy is inferred."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e07","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-seven-dreams-and-madness-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide places Hera’s council hearing on Coruscant; this does not mean Ahsoka visits Coruscant."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e07","worldId":"peridea","worldName":"Peridea","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-seven-dreams-and-madness-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide explicitly places Ezra and Sabine traveling with the Noti on Peridea."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e08","worldId":"peridea","worldName":"Peridea","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/ahsoka-part-8-the-jedi-the-witch-and-the-warlord-highlights","note":"The episode highlights explicitly place Shin entering the bandit camp on Peridea."},{"itemId":"ahsoka-s01e08","worldId":"dathomir","worldName":"Dathomir","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/ahsoka/part-eight-the-jedi-the-witch-and-the-warlord-episode-guide","note":"The episode guide confirms Thrawn arriving at Dathomir with his cargo. This is an arrival/orbital association, not a claimed surface visit by Ahsoka."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"lahmu","worldName":"Lah’mu","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The film-specific guide identifies Lah’mu as the Erso family’s hiding place. Earlier scenes remain part of the complete film."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"ring-of-kafrene","worldName":"Ring of Kafrene","locationKind":"asteroid-outpost","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The film-specific guide describes the trading outpost built between two asteroids. This is not a planet or a sourced map coordinate."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"wobani","worldName":"Wobani","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The guide explicitly includes Wobani’s Imperial labor camps among the film’s settings."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"jedha","worldName":"Jedha","locationKind":"moon","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The film-specific guide identifies the holy moon Jedha, distinct from its parent NaJedha."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"eadu","worldName":"Eadu","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The film-specific guide identifies Eadu and its Imperial kyber refining facility."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"yavin","worldName":"Yavin 4","locationKind":"moon","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The guide explicitly includes the fourth moon of Yavin among the film’s settings; this is not the parent gas giant."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"mustafar","worldName":"Mustafar","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/databank/vader-s-castle","note":"Vader’s Castle Databank locates the castle on Mustafar and explicitly lists Rogue One under appearances."},{"itemId":"rogue-one","worldId":"scarif","worldName":"Scarif","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/where-in-the-galaxy-are-the-worlds-of-rogue-one","note":"The film-specific guide identifies Scarif and the Imperial Citadel Tower storing the Death Star plans."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e01","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-1-highlights","note":"The chapter commentary explicitly places the Sarlacc escape and Tusken memories on Tatooine. Earlier scenes remain within the chapter; this association does not date every scene to the present."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e02","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/series/the-book-of-boba-fett/chapter-2-tribes-of-tatooine-episode-guide","note":"The exact chapter synopsis identifies Tatooine. Present-day and remembered events remain grouped at the title level."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e03","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-3-highlights","note":"The commentary places Fett’s rule and the Mos Espa dispute on Tatooine and separately identifies his Tusken flashbacks."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e04","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-4-highlights","note":"The chapter article locates Fett’s search and Fennec’s rescue on Tatooine, with the past distinguished from the present-day alliance."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e05","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-5-story-gallery","context":"surface","note":"Story-gallery captions 6 and 9 explicitly place Din’s arrival and starfighter test over Tatooine. Naboo describes the craft’s origin, not a Naboo visit."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e05","worldId":"glavis-ringworld","worldName":"Glavis Ringworld","locationKind":"space-station","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-5-story-gallery","note":"Story-gallery caption 2 explicitly names the Glavis Ringworld as Din collects payment and returns to the covert. Station identity is independently supported by its Databank; no map position is established."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e05","worldId":"mandalore","worldName":"Mandalore","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-5-highlights","context":"flashback","note":"Highlight 2 describes images of the Imperial bombardment of Mandalore. This is a historical destruction sequence, not Din traveling there in this chapter."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e06","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-6-story-gallery","context":"surface","note":"Story-gallery captions 1 and 6 explicitly locate Cobb Vanth’s confrontation and Din’s arrival at Fett’s palace on Tatooine."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e06","worldId":"coruscant","worldName":"Coruscant","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-6-highlights","context":"flashback","note":"Highlight 2 explicitly places Grogu’s remembered Order 66 scene in the Coruscant Temple; this is not a present-day visit."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e06","worldId":"luke-jedi-school","worldName":"Luke’s Jedi school","locationKind":"surface-site","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-6-highlights","context":"surface","note":"The chapter commentary identifies the future Jedi school where Luke trains Grogu. The reviewed source does not name its planet; no Ossus identity, parent, or coordinate is inferred."},{"itemId":"boba-fett-s01e07","worldId":"tatooine","worldName":"Tatooine","locationKind":"planet","sourceUrl":"https://www.starwars.com/news/the-book-of-boba-fett-chapter-7-highlights","context":"surface","note":"The finale commentary explicitly places the conflict on Tatooine and describes Grogu’s arrival at Peli Motto’s shop."}]'::jsonb);
DO $publication$
BEGIN
 IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM atlas_publications WHERE id='initial-2026-11-07') THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Required initial publication missing'; END IF;
 IF (SELECT count(*) FROM atlas_works) <> 201 OR (SELECT count(*) FROM atlas_worlds) <> 76 THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Catalog/map baseline differs from reviewed publication'; END IF;
 IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM desired_appearances d LEFT JOIN atlas_works w ON w.id=d.work_id WHERE w.id IS NULL) THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Appearance references an unknown work'; END IF;
 IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM atlas_appearances a LEFT JOIN desired_appearances d USING(work_id,world_id) WHERE d.work_id IS NULL OR a.payload IS DISTINCT FROM d.payload) THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Existing appearance evidence conflicts with reviewed dataset'; END IF;
 IF EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM atlas_publications WHERE id='catalog-sha256-5030e615755a3fda053547a45c2c01f9a3b8a87c59c374219bf2e4dd43e1a601' AND payload IS DISTINCT FROM '{"id":"catalog-sha256-5030e615755a3fda053547a45c2c01f9a3b8a87c59c374219bf2e4dd43e1a601","sha256":"45607a19ba5af7aa54986911d6de689c29635d182b2a583049f5c4a6665a2388","works":201,"worlds":76,"appearances":302,"coveredTitles":195,"worldsSha256":"ee7e18f1b2794b5ca8839f6070bdd0645d4bf5d9363a98df0da972fcce35eb0e","catalogSha256":"4270042d9cd9a18f01e56a568743de86b258aecc26304e5efd57b84d9ee8d199","sequencesSha256":"b96680cc20f6b96d4134215b38bb783f3f453bfa6fb9f84154778864d30d7573","sequences":7}'::jsonb) THEN RAISE EXCEPTION 'Publication identity already has different metadata'; END IF;
END $publication$;
